# Canonical identities for `git shortlog`, `git log` and every tool that reads them.
#
# Two reasons this file exists, and the second is the load-bearing one:
#
# 1. One person should appear once. `git shortlog -sne` listed "Joshua Thompson"
#    twice, under two addresses, which makes a solo project look like two people who
#    each did half the work.
#
# 2. It moves a personal address OUT of what tooling displays. Eight early commits
#    carry a personal inbox in their author metadata. That cannot be removed without
#    rewriting history, and rewriting public history to hide an address that is
#    already published would be a lot of breakage for no gain. Mapping it here means
#    `git log`, `git shortlog`, GitHub's contributor views and anything else honouring
#    .mailmap all render the GitHub noreply address instead. The raw commit objects
#    still hold the original — this is presentation, not redaction, and claiming
#    otherwise would be the kind of overstatement this repo's docs try to avoid.
#
# Format: <canonical name and email> <email to rewrite>

Joshua Thompson <74799121+JayMTea@users.noreply.github.com> <74799121+JayMTea@users.noreply.github.com>
Joshua Thompson <74799121+JayMTea@users.noreply.github.com> <74799121+JayMTea@users.noreply.github.com>

# Automation, so it is never mistaken for a human contributor. `Ava (auto-sync)` is
# this repo's own pre-commit hook regenerating diagrams — it is the project writing to
# itself, and reading it as an author overstates the contributor count.
Ava (auto-sync) <ava@localhost> <ava@localhost>
dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
